    {
      "id": "cnfotuc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Radius and General Facts about the Earth"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth's interior is structured into three concentric layers: Crust, Mantle, and Core.",
        "The Crust is divided into thicker, less dense Continental Crust (SIAL) and thinner, denser Oceanic Crust (SIMA).",
        "The Mantle contains the Asthenosphere, a semi-fluid zone responsible for tectonic plate movements.",
        "The Core consists of a liquid Outer Core and a solid Inner Core composed primarily of Nickel and Iron (NIFE).",
        "Seismic discontinuities mark abrupt changes in density and seismic wave velocity between layers."
      ],
      "id": "rest9ke"
    },
